Current Framework Limitation
Your current framework treats each agent as a standalone entity. This works for simple workflows but breaks down for complex tasks:

Current Reality:
- One agent = One workflow
- Flat orchestration
- No concept of agent teams
- No hierarchical coordination

Proposed Solutions
Option 1: Project Manager Pattern (Your Suggestion)

topic_analysis_pm:
  type: project-manager
  manages:
    - date_extractor_agent
    - entity_extractor_agent
    - number_parser_agent
    - verification_agent

  workflow:
    coordinate_extraction:
      action: fan_out
      sub_tasks:
        - agent: date_extractor
        - agent: entity_extractor
        - agent: number_parser

    verify_results:
      action: send_to_agent
      agent: verification_agent


Pros:

Clear hierarchy
Single point of contact
Easier monitoring

Cons:

PM becomes bottleneck
Complex state management
Nested orchestration complexity

Option 2: Agent Families/Squads

agent_family_definition:
  name: structured_extraction_squad
  members:
    - date_extractor
    - entity_extractor
    - number_parser
    - result_merger

  coordination: peer_to_peer
  shared_context: true

  interface:
    input: raw_text
    output: structured_data

// New concept: AgentFamily
type AgentFamily struct {
    FamilyID     string
    Members      []AgentInstance
    SharedState  SharedMemory
    Coordinator  CoordinationType // peer_to_peer, hierarchical, consensus
}

