Critical Analysis
The Real Problem: Workflow Complexity
Single Agent Workflow:
  steps: 3-5
  complexity: manageable

Topic Analysis Workflow:
  steps: 50+
  parallel_branches: 10+
  conditional_logic: heavy
  complexity: overwhelming

What We Actually Need: Workflow Composition
// Workflow as a first-class concept
type WorkflowDefinition struct {
    ID          string
    Name        string
    SubWorkflows []WorkflowDefinition  // Can contain other workflows
    AgentPool   []AgentInstance       // Available agents
    Coordination CoordinationStrategy
}

// Example: Hierarchical workflows
MainWorkflow
├── DataCollectionWorkflow
│   ├── NewsAPIWorkflow
│   ├── SocialMediaWorkflow
│   └── RSSWorkflow
├── ExtractionWorkflow
│   ├── DateExtractionWorkflow
│   └── EntityExtractionWorkflow
└── AnalysisWorkflow

Recommended Architecture: Hybrid Approach
1. Service Agents (Stateless, Reusable)

# These are like microservices
date_extractor_service:
  type: service-agent
  stateless: true
  endpoint: extract_dates
  can_be_called_by: any_workflow

entity_extractor_service:
  type: service-agent
  stateless: true
  endpoint: extract_entities
  can_be_called_by: any_workflow

2. Coordinator Agents (Stateful, Orchestrating)

topic_analysis_coordinator:
  type: coordinator-agent
  workflow:
    collect_data:
      parallel:
        - call: news_collector_service
        - call: social_collector_service

    extract_structure:
      parallel:
        - call: date_extractor_service
        - call: entity_extractor_service

    merge_results:
      action: merge_structured_data

3. Agent Pools (Load Balanced)
extraction_pool:
  agents:
    - date_extractor_1
    - date_extractor_2
    - date_extractor_3

  load_balancer: round_robin
  scaling: auto

