3. Registry Pattern for Service Agents

type ServiceRegistry struct {
    mu sync.RWMutex
    services map[string]ServiceAgent
}

func (r *ServiceRegistry) Call(serviceName string, input interface{}) (interface{}, error) {
    service, exists := r.services[serviceName]
    if !exists {
        return nil, fmt.Errorf("service not found: %s", serviceName)
    }

    return service.Execute(input)
}

Practical Migration Path
Phase 1: Service Agents (Week 1)
Convert stateless operations to service agents:

Date extraction
Entity extraction
Number parsing
Deduplication

Phase 2: Composite Workflows (Week 2)
Allow workflows to call other workflows:
main_workflow:
  steps:
    collect:
      action: invoke_workflow
      workflow_id: data_collection_workflow

    analyze:
      action: invoke_workflow
      workflow_id: analysis_workflow

Phase 3: Agent Groups (Week 3-4)
Implement formal agent groups:

Shared context
Group messaging
Collective decision making

The Critical Decision
Do you want:
A) Hierarchical (PM pattern)

Easier to understand
Single point of failure
Clear accountability

B) Peer-to-peer (Squad pattern)

More resilient
Complex coordination
Distributed decision making

C) Service-oriented (Microservices pattern)

Maximum reusability
Clear interfaces
Easier testing

My Recommendation: Start with C (Service-oriented), then add B (Squad pattern) for complex coordinations. This gives you:

Reusable components
Clean architecture
Flexibility to compose
Natural evolution path

